# Liberty Pharmacy — environment template
# Copy to .env.local and fill in. NEVER commit .env.local.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Patient data encryption — REQUIRED for the portal register/login features.
# 32-byte hex key used for AES-256-GCM field-level encryption of PHI at rest.
# Generate with:  openssl rand -hex 32
# In production, source this from a managed secret store (never a file).
# Rotating it requires re-encrypting existing patient rows.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PHI_ENCRYPTION_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OTP email delivery — Gmail SMTP (free; demo/fake-data phase ONLY).
# Consumer Gmail has no BAA: swap to a BAA-covered provider (AWS SES) before
# real patients enroll. Setup:
#   1. On the Google account: enable 2-Step Verification.
#   2. Google Account -> Security -> App passwords -> create one for "Mail".
#   3. Paste the 16-character app password below (NOT your Gmail password).
# Unset = dev prints codes to the server console; production refuses to send.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GMAIL_USER=you@gmail.com
# GMAIL_APP_PASSWORD=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Public origin used to build password-reset links in emails.
# Leave unset in local dev (the request's own origin is used). Set this in
# production — behind a proxy the request origin may be an internal address,
# which would email patients an unreachable link.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# APP_BASE_URL=https://libertypharmacyatx.com

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DRX integration (future) — leave unset until the integration phase.
# A signed BAA with DRX is REQUIRED before any PHI flows through these APIs.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Public patient storefront (safe for the browser), e.g.:
# NEXT_PUBLIC_DRX_STORE_URL=https://liberty.drxrefill.com

# Server-only API access — never prefix these with NEXT_PUBLIC_.
# DRX_API_BASE_URL=
# DRX_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Contact form delivery (future).
# The contact API route currently logs nothing and stores nothing.
# When wiring up email delivery, use a HIPAA-eligible provider under BAA
# (e.g. Paubox, or AWS SES within a BAA-covered account).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CONTACT_FORWARD_EMAIL=
# EMAIL_PROVIDER_API_KEY=
